{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>From that land</b> — when he ruled over it, \"went out Asshur\" — its interpretation is: he went out to Asshur, for Asshur was of the sons of Shem. This is like the language of \"and it went out to Hazar Addar and passed on to Atzmon\" (Numbers 34:4), \"and Og king of Bashan went out toward us, to Edrei\" (Deuteronomy 3:1), \"and he shall return to his land with great substance\" (Daniel 11:28), and many similar. Therefore the land of Asshur is called \"the land of Nimrod,\" as it is stated (Micah 5:5), \"and they shall shepherd Asshur with the sword, and the land of Nimrod at its gates\" — and \"the land of Nimrod\" alludes to Nineveh and Rehoboth Ir and Calah. And Scripture further recounts his might, that he was a mighty hunter, to show that he prevailed even over the beasts and hunted them. And it says \"before YHWH\" to exaggerate, that under all the heavens there was none like him in might. Similarly, \"and the earth was corrupted before Elohim\" (Genesis 6:11) — for all that is before Him on earth was corrupted, in the sense of \"and that soul shall be cut off from before Me\" (Leviticus 22:3), for in every place He is before it:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:27:06.819473605Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}